option=allowed:the public script announces 1.1.1.1/32 and 3.3.3.3/32 with next-hop 127.0.0.1 to neighbor 127.0.0.1, and on this loopback session 127.0.0.1 is the peer's own address; RFC 4271 Section 5.1.3 says "A route originated by a BGP speaker SHALL NOT be advertised to a peer using an address of that peer as NEXT_HOP", so ze withholds both and logs why, then stops on the private script's `shutdown` one second later with Cease 6/2, Administrative Shutdown (the ExaBGP 6.0 copy, test/exabgp-compat/api/api-multiple-api.ci, moves the neighbor to 127.0.0.2 for the same reason)
